From: Hyunho Song <songhh06101@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:37:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ipc/msg: serialize receive permission checks with IPC_SET

do_msgrcv() checks read permission before taking the queue lock.  IPC_SET
can revoke access after that check and before the receiver joins
q_receivers.  It then misses the IPC_SET wakeup and can receive a later
message despite losing access.

Take the queue lock before the receive loop so the permission check,
message lookup and insertion into q_receivers are serialized with IPC_SET.
The receiver releases the lock before sleeping.  On an -EAGAIN wakeup it
reacquires the lock, removes itself from q_receivers, and keeps the lock
for the next permission check.  The earlier revision [1] unlocked at the
bottom of the loop only to lock again at the top.

Signed-off-by: Hyunho Song <songhh06101@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Reported-by: Hyunho Song <songhh06101@gmail.com>
Suggested-by: Manfred Spraul <manfred@colorfullife.com>
Reviewed-by: Manfred Spraul <manfred@colorfullife.com>
Tested-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Davidlohr Bueso <dave@stgolabs.net>
Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org>

 ipc/msg.c |    7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
---
 ipc/msg.c | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ipc/msg.c b/ipc/msg.c
index d985fecde74fc..4630645d37bf2 100644
--- a/ipc/msg.c
+++ b/ipc/msg.c
@@ -1132,14 +1132,13 @@ static long do_msgrcv(int msqid, void __user *buf, size_t bufsz, long msgtyp, in
 		return PTR_ERR(msq);
 	}
 
+	ipc_lock_object(&msq->q_perm);
 	for (;;) {
 		struct msg_receiver msr_d;
 
 		msg = ERR_PTR(-EACCES);
 		if (ipcperms(ns, &msq->q_perm, S_IRUGO))
-			goto out_unlock1;
-
-		ipc_lock_object(&msq->q_perm);
+			goto out_unlock0;
 
 		/* raced with RMID? */
 		if (!ipc_valid_object(&msq->q_perm)) {
@@ -1248,8 +1247,6 @@ static long do_msgrcv(int msqid, void __user *buf, size_t bufsz, long msgtyp, in
 			msg = ERR_PTR(-ERESTARTNOHAND);
 			goto out_unlock0;
 		}
-
-		ipc_unlock_object(&msq->q_perm);
 	}
 
 out_unlock0:
-- 
2.47.3

